From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Grische <github@grische.xyz>
Date: Mon, 24 Aug 2026 12:13:16 +0200
Subject: MIPS: dts: intel-mips: name the kernel slots by position

Both boards carry two 8 MiB kernel slots, at 0x500000 and 0xd00000, and
the boot-loader environment's linux_fs_start selects between them: 0
picks the first, 1 the second, and the vendor kernel reads the same
variable. Both slots are defined on every board of
this family, at the same offsets, and the definitions are byte-identical
between the FRITZ!Box 7560 and the FRITZ!Box 7590.

The labels claimed to know which slot was in use -- "kernel" for the
active one, "reserved-kernel" for the other -- and put them opposite ways
round on the two boards. That cannot be right in a fixed-partitions map,
because linux_fs_start is not a property of the board. It is runtime
state that the boot loader may change on its own, so a map that pins a
role is wrong for any unit whose selector has ever moved -- including a
unit the map was correct for when it was written.

Name the slots by position instead and let the code that writes them
decide what to do about it. This also makes the two boards' partition
maps identical except for the ubi size, which is what the hardware
actually looks like.

The FRITZ!Box 7590's comment additionally instructed the reader to assert
linux_fs_start == 1 before flashing. Delete it: it documents an
assumption this change removes.

Assisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-5
Signed-off-by: Grische <github@grische.xyz>

diff --git a/arch/mips/boot/dts/intel-mips/seale_avm_fritz7560.dts b/arch/mips/boot/dts/intel-mips/seale_avm_fritz7560.dts
index e198da969689..fef3ebdf207d 100644
--- a/arch/mips/boot/dts/intel-mips/seale_avm_fritz7560.dts
+++ b/arch/mips/boot/dts/intel-mips/seale_avm_fritz7560.dts
@@ -204,15 +204,18 @@ partition@100000 {
 			read-only;
 		};
 
-		/* Primary kernel slot. Written by sysupgrade. */
+		/*
+		 * The two 8 MiB kernel slots. The labels name slots, not
+		 * roles: the boot loader rewrites the selector, so no label
+		 * may claim to be the active one.
+		 */
 		partition@500000 {
-			label = "kernel";
+			label = "kernel0";
 			reg = <0x500000 0x800000>;
 		};
 
-		/* AVM secondary/recovery kernel slot. Written by sysupgrade. */
 		partition@d00000 {
-			label = "reserved-kernel";
+			label = "kernel1";
 			reg = <0xd00000 0x800000>;
 		};
 
diff --git a/arch/mips/boot/dts/intel-mips/seale_avm_fritz7590.dts b/arch/mips/boot/dts/intel-mips/seale_avm_fritz7590.dts
index 5e32ec74d668..3fef5173eff2 100644
--- a/arch/mips/boot/dts/intel-mips/seale_avm_fritz7590.dts
+++ b/arch/mips/boot/dts/intel-mips/seale_avm_fritz7590.dts
@@ -181,15 +181,19 @@ partition@100000 {
 			read-only;
 		};
 
-		/* Inactive kernel slot 0. Written by sysupgrade. */
+		/*
+		 * Two 8 MiB kernel slots, named by position: which one is
+		 * active is boot-loader run-time state (its linux_fs_start
+		 * selects between them), so no label may claim to be the
+		 * active one.
+		 */
 		partition@500000 {
-			label = "reserved-kernel";
+			label = "kernel0";
 			reg = <0x500000 0x800000>;
 		};
 
-		/* Active kernel slot 1 -- the one EVA boots on this unit. */
 		partition@d00000 {
-			label = "kernel";
+			label = "kernel1";
 			reg = <0xd00000 0x800000>;
 		};
 
